WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
Also, we're tracking

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.301
new developments

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.535
overnight as Ukraine

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.104
may be getting one step closer

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.438
to receiving those U.S.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.507
made F-16 fighter jets.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.542
Officials are now telling CNN

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.044
that the Biden administration

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.445
has signaled to European

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.180
allies that the US would approve

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.082
the export of the jets to Ukraine

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.716
if that's

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.718
what they decide to do with their supply.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.286
The White House has been under increasing

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.255
pressure from allies and members

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.523
of Congress to help Ukraine

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.657
secure the planes

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.358
as Russia's

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.159
aerial attacks

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.660
have only continued to intensify,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.396
especially this month alone.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.263
CNN's insatiable

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.931
trend is live at the Pentagon.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.999
Natasha, obviously

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.768
we've seen the US initially say,

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.369
you know,
we're not going to send tanks,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.571
we're not going to send rocket launchers,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.706
we're not going to send these air

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.740
defense missiles

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.941
only to later released

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.076
and so the question is,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:43.777
is that what we think

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:44.677
is going to happen here?

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:46.379
Yeah, there

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.281
certainly have been many lines

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.382
that the administration said it

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.917
previously would not cross, that

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.285
it has now crossed

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.386
with regard to many weapons

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.320
it has sent to Ukraine.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.388
But right now,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.990
we're still seeing a lot of reluctance

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.425
by the US to signal

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.659
that it would send its own

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.428
F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:01.995
Of course,

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.197
the US has a large stockpile of those.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.698
Instead, they are telling

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.800
us, officials are telling us

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.501
that they will not block

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.436
European allies

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.104
who have these supply of F-16

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.571
fighter jets

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.872
from exporting them

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.207
to Ukraine themselves,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.875
if that is what they want to do.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.043
And this is really significant

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.512
because the US has to approve

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.581
any transfer of these F-16 jets

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.582
to Ukraine

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.017
or to any third country at all

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.286
because of sensitive US technology

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.587
that is in those jets.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.155
So previously it was unclear

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.356
whether the administration

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.424
would approve

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.359
the export of these fighter jets.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.394
Now we are hearing that

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:35.829
they have signaled to the allies

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.329
that if that is

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.730
what they want to do with their jets,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.999
then the US is not going to stand

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:40.667
in their way.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.135
And this is really significant also

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.037
because the Ukrainians

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.238
without these fighter jets,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.239
they have had to improvise.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.540
We are told that the Ukrainians

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.542
have used a Patriot missile

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.677
at least once

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.277
to shoot down

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.445
a Russian fighter jet,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.947
which is not necessarily

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.315
what they're designed to do.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.150
So with these jets, the administration

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.351
and officials argue

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.385
it will be a lot easier

00:01:59.385 --> 00:01:59.752
for them

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.387
to counter the Russian jets

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.455
potentially gain

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.756
superiority in their skies.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:04.858
Now, all of this comes

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.559
as the administration is telling us

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:06.860
that there was

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.361
actually an accounting error

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:11.498
in the military aid funding

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.066
over the last couple of months

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.067
that they have just discovered

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:14.934
that actually frees up

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.803
an additional $3 billion

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.937
in draw down authorities.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.906
So the Ukrainians really anticipating

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.108
that a boon to U.S.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:22.842
aid to

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:23.409
the Ukrainians

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.044
could be coming quite soon. Caitlin.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:25.778
Yeah, and I know

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.946
lawmakers have a lot of questions

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.048
about how that accounting error happened

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:29.916
but we'll get to that.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.117
But also, this other story

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.018
that's on the front page

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.453
of The Washington Post today

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.420
caught my eye.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.822
There was a missile

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.422
or a strike

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.957
that happened in Syria earlier

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.926
this month that the US said

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.096
took out an influential al Qaeda leader.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.497
And now we're hearing from

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.632
Central Central Command

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.200
that they are investigating it, saying

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.269
it may have resulted in a civilian

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.436
that was killed in Syria.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.437
What do you know about this?

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.339
Yeah, Caitlin.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:53.740
So according

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.941
to a statement overnight

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:55.708
from Central Command,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.876
they are investigating

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.912
whether a air strike or a U.S.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.980
airstrike on May 3rd in northwest Syria

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.949
actually did not kill a senior

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.417
Al Qaida leader as Central

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.919
Command had previously stated

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:06.786
in a tweet

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.687
earlier this month,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.888
but that it actually resulted

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.590
in the death of a civilian.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.792
Now, it had been very unclear earlier

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.893
this month when Central Command

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.494
announced that

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.029
they had conducted this strike.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.497
Who the target actually was,

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.132
because they had never identified

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.100
the supposed senior al Qaeda leader

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.702
that they had allegedly killed.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.037
Well, now we're learning

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.438
that it may not have been a senior

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.473
al Qaeda figure at all that they killed,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.342
but it was actually a civilian farmer.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.710
So they are investigating

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.344
that now, Caitlin,

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.046
and we'll wait for those results.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.481
Yeah,
and certainly why people ask for evidence

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.883
when they both felt something like this.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.751
Natasha, keep us updated thank you.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:39.485
Joining us now for

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:40.954
the military perspective on

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.021
this is retired Air

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.523
Force Colonel Cedric Leighton,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.057
a CNN

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.858
military analyst and former member,

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:46.726
I should note, of the Joint

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.628
Chiefs of Staff at the Pentagon.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:49.762
Thank you so much for being here.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.564
Obviously, the F-16 is something

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.566
we've been talking about for so long,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.667
whether or not

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.501
they are going to be able

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.004
to get them develop this air superiority

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:58.871
they've not been.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.074
Ukraine has not been able to do so far.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.809
But the pushback we've heard from

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.743
the US has been

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.578
it takes so long

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:06.412
to train

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.648
the Ukrainian forces on these F-16s.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:09.682
What's the sense

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.818
of how it could help, though?

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.453
Yeah, that's a great question, Caitlin.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.521
So let's take a look at the F-16,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.557
because what you're looking at here

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.126
is a very versatile aircraft.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.261
And, you know,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.695
when you see what it can do,

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.230
I mean, it can fly at 1500

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:24.964
miles per hour.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:25.999
It uses

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.234
what are known as radiation detection

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.603
and target to target air defense systems.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.005
So this is very important

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.307
because what it's going to be able to do

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.742
is it's going to be able to go

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.746
after Russian air defense areas,

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:40.380
such as the AC

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.781
300 of the missile system

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.750
that's there, the S-400 potentially.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.618
But those are also very dangerous weapons

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.153
for this kind of an aircraft.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.222
It is not a stealth fighter.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.590
It has a 20 millimeter gun.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.458
It's basically an air to air

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.228
and an air to ground combat platform.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.397
And that's one of the main reasons,

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.898
because of its versatility,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.134
that the Ukrainians want this aircraft.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.835
Yeah, very versatile, obviously,

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.636
something they could use.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.338
We've seen how they've tried to make up

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.639
for not having them.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.508
The new reporting from CNN

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.442
is that the U.S.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.643
is signaling to allies

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.313
that it may allow the export of F-16s,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.614
which would allow other countries

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.049
that have these

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.216
obviously made in the US

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.985
to be able to send them to Ukraine.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.953
Which countries is it exactly that

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:21.954
that have the F-16s

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.056
that could have the capability

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.191
of potentially sending them?

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.393
So these are the countries in NATO,

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.995
besides the United States,

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.397
that actually fly the F-16.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:32.999
Everyone from Turkey and Greece

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.867
all the way up through Romania, Poland,

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:35.635
and then of course,

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.836
the Scandinavian countries

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.137
of Norway, Denmark,

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.505
and then the Benelux,

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.074
Netherlands and Belgium.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:43.009
So these countries are critical

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:43.643
for this

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.745
one country that has made that transition

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:48.214
very effectively from Soviet

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.017
era fighters to the F-16 is Poland.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:52.452
Another one is Romania.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.020
So these two countries would be

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.455
the most likely ones

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:57.023
to help with that transition,

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.324
because they're also interested

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.393
in getting newer generation fighters

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.362
that are even newer than the F-16.

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.629
And this would be one way to do

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.165
that, provided their F-16 arms to Ukraine

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.567
and then be able to use

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:08.334
for the Ukrainians,

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.836
be able to use them against

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.404
Russian targets.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.005
Yeah, with these at sixes,

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.674
I've talked to people at the Pentagon

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.877
about the reluctance to say whether U.S.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:18.778
will allow U.S.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.646
allies to export theirs

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.815
or we ourselves will send them.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:23.750
But it's also an argument

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.585
we heard about the tanks,

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.220
about other pieces of equipment

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.655
that they did eventually send to Ukraine.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.224
What's your sense of what they'll

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.959
what they'll do here?

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.026
So what I think they're going to do,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.895
Caitlin, is, you know,

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.097
looking at all the different platforms

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.065
and weapon systems

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.067
that we have provided to the Ukrainians,

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.669
you know, everything from anti-aircraft

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.705
missiles and Stinger varieties.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.707
155 millimeter Howitzers,

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.642
the drones, the switchblade drones.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.843
And of course, as you mentioned,

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.578
the tanks, the Patriot missiles,

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.947
all of those become important packages.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:55.715
So my sense

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.316
is that what they're going to do

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.584
is they're going to let

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.920
the Ukrainians have the F-16.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.255
You'd mentioned earlier

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.156
that one of the key

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:05.391
things is training pilots.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.993
Two countries have indicated

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.628
that they would like to train

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.930
the Ukrainians on Western platforms.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.098
Those would be the Netherlands

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.499
and the United Kingdom.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.635
And that could very well

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.669
make the difference.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:17.904
The training system

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.605
that we currently have in place

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.207
takes about nine months

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.008
for most people

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.543
to train into the F-16

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:26.045
and then be proficient in that aircraft.

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:28.080
The Ukrainians might be able to do it

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.682
within 69 days

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.385
if they just move from their platforms.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.152
The SOVIET-ERA

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:36.923
MiG 29 and SU 27 into the F-16.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.891
They won't be completely proficient

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.193
after that time frame.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.627
But it is something that they could

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:42.862
potentially do

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:43.563
given the fact

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.897
that they have a lot of combat

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.432
experience already.

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:46.833
And all of

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:48.434
this is being discussed in Japan

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.969
right now. So we'll see what they decide.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.237
A US made Patriot

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.138
air defense system

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.706
is reportedly fully back up

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:54.240
and running

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.308
after taking damage

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:56.642
during Russian missile strikes

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.810
in Ukraine.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.812
Moscow claimed its hypersonic missiles

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:00.980
hit a Patriot battery

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.082
during an attack near Keefe on Tuesday.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.650
But according to the Pentagon,

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.452
that didn't make much of a difference.

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.555
So for more specifics,

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:10.723
on the
Patriot itself,

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:13.326
I would refer you to the Ukrainians.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.494
What I can confirm

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:17.163
is that one Patriot system was damaged,

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.598
but it has now been fixed

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:20.867
and is fully fully back and operational.

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:22.835
Multiple U.S.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:23.936
officials told CNN

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.538
the damage on the Patriot battery

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:27.640
similar to this one was only minor.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:28.875
It's still unclear

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:29.942
if the damage was caused

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.043
by a missile strike

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:32.278
or from falling debris.

